WEBVTT

00:06.507 --> 00:08.258
…and the once uninhabited island,

00:08.342 --> 00:11.720
42 nautical miles from the coast
of colonial New England,

00:12.304 --> 00:14.515
came to be known as Widow's Bay.

00:15.265 --> 00:18.310
Now home to over 3,000 residents,

00:18.393 --> 00:22.606
a town comprised
of fishermen, families, and friends,

00:22.689 --> 00:24.942
all thanks to one man.

00:25.025 --> 00:27.569
Thank you for joining us
for Richard Warren's journey

00:27.653 --> 00:29.154
from humble tradesmen

00:29.238 --> 00:32.783
to the first Reeve Prime
and Lord Island Protector,

00:32.866 --> 00:37.204
an office the town
now colloquially refers to as "Mayor."

00:49.132 --> 00:54.096
And here's Richard the widower with his…
his adoring second wife, Sarah Warren.

00:54.680 --> 00:57.057
She's seen here
preparing the evening meal.

00:57.558 --> 00:59.476
We also have her journal.

01:00.102 --> 01:02.229
So, where are you all from?

01:03.021 --> 01:05.065
We've never had so many visitors.

01:40.809 --> 01:42.644
Come on out tonight

01:42.728 --> 01:48.525
And we'll lead the others
On a ride through paradise

01:48.609 --> 01:53.238
And if you feel all right
Then we can be lovers…

01:56.200 --> 01:58.577
There there's no cell reception
on the island.

01:59.620 --> 02:00.621
Thanks.

02:02.039 --> 02:03.040
Can I help?

02:04.416 --> 02:05.751
No, I have a map. Thanks.

02:06.251 --> 02:07.419
Yeah, I made it.

02:07.503 --> 02:09.045
Warning, it's not to scale.

02:10.631 --> 02:11.882
I'm sorry, I'm the mayor.

02:12.633 --> 02:14.843
My photo's on page four.

02:20.849 --> 02:21.850
Well, that's fun.

02:23.310 --> 02:25.979
Well then you should probably know
the map isn't the problem,

02:26.563 --> 02:27.773
it's your street signs.

02:28.607 --> 02:31.401
Unless this actually is "Dickhole Street"?

02:32.819 --> 02:33.862
It's not.

02:35.447 --> 02:37.157
Where are you headed?
Can I offer you a ride?

02:39.660 --> 02:40.661
All right. Just…

02:41.370 --> 02:42.663
don't murder me.

02:45.916 --> 02:48.335
We got in last night,
but we just went to bed.

02:48.919 --> 02:50.838
There was a time
we would have picked Vegas,

02:50.921 --> 02:54.967
but these days a bachelorette in a place
like this is a little more our speed.

02:56.093 --> 02:57.928
- You getting married?
- Me? No.

02:59.304 --> 03:00.889
No, just a bridesmaid.

03:02.057 --> 03:03.308
We're staying at the Inn.

03:04.768 --> 03:06.144
How was your stay?

03:06.854 --> 03:08.397
It's nice. It's quaint.

03:08.480 --> 03:09.481
- Great.
- Yeah.

03:10.357 --> 03:11.984
Man, if I lived here,

03:12.067 --> 03:14.987
I would go to the beach with a coffee
and a crossword every morning.

03:15.863 --> 03:17.322
Then you should go
to the opening tomorrow.

03:17.406 --> 03:19.575
I'm doing the inaugural swim.

03:21.243 --> 03:22.953
It's just one of the island traditions.

03:23.036 --> 03:25.122
The mayor swims in the ocean every year

03:25.205 --> 03:27.040
to show that it's safe from…

03:28.292 --> 03:30.085
the island's history of ocean…

03:31.962 --> 03:33.213
dangers.

03:33.297 --> 03:34.506
- Interesting.
- Yeah.

03:35.007 --> 03:38.468
We're also hosting
a Sunset Cocktails event after.

03:39.011 --> 03:41.763
I mean, if you and your friends
are looking for some nightlife.

03:42.264 --> 03:46.310
Tonight the girls were talking
about going to Barnabus Tavern.

03:46.393 --> 03:47.978
- It's supposed to be a dive bar.
- Yeah.

03:48.061 --> 03:49.521
Do you… do you go there?

03:50.856 --> 03:51.857
Yeah, sometimes.

03:53.358 --> 03:55.152
Well, maybe I'll see you there then.

03:56.612 --> 03:58.280
Yeah. Yeah. Maybe.

04:02.868 --> 04:05.370
Well, some of the cash businesses downtown

04:05.454 --> 04:07.497
are balking at the idea
of a city sales tax.

04:07.581 --> 04:09.458
They said… actually they said,

04:09.958 --> 04:12.794
"If you want this blood money,
you gotta come and get it yourself,"

04:12.878 --> 04:13.962
which felt threatening.

04:14.046 --> 04:16.839
So… I don't know, I'm at a loss.
What do you think, Tom?

04:20.469 --> 04:22.095
Yeah. Yeah.

04:22.179 --> 04:24.473
No, of course. Yeah, that's great.

04:24.556 --> 04:28.477
Hey, are we getting the word out
about the sunset cocktails?

04:29.228 --> 04:31.855
I just feel like no one knows about it.

04:33.732 --> 04:35.484
I have personally been spreading the word

04:35.567 --> 04:38.695
and Rosemary's been passing out flyers
all morning.

04:38.779 --> 04:41.073
Yeah, I think she's
just been smoking outside.

04:41.156 --> 04:43.700
You really need to stay on top of this,
'cause I spoke to a woman,

04:43.784 --> 04:44.952
hadn't heard about any of it.

04:46.036 --> 04:47.788
- What woman?
- Just a woman.

04:48.580 --> 04:50.541
- Where did you speak to her?
- In my car.

04:50.624 --> 04:51.750
I don't understand.

04:51.834 --> 04:53.585
Well, she was lost,

04:53.669 --> 04:56.797
so I offered her a ride 'cause
it seemed like the right thing to do.

04:57.297 --> 04:59.633
- Of course. Excuse me.
- That's fine.

04:59.716 --> 05:03.887
Anyway, let's just make sure
every accommodation has all the info.

05:03.971 --> 05:07.683
Restaurants too.
And… I also want to talk about music.

05:07.766 --> 05:09.852
What music we're going to play
when I walk from the platform

05:09.935 --> 05:12.563
to the ocean for the swim,
because I don't want that to be awkward.

05:12.646 --> 05:15.357
- Was she attractive?
- I didn't notice one way or the other.

05:15.983 --> 05:18.443
- How old was she?
- She was… She was age-appropriate.

05:20.529 --> 05:23.323
What an odd way to describe someone
who you're just giving a ride.

05:26.034 --> 05:27.995
Well, Patricia, as mayor,

05:28.871 --> 05:31.123
the safety of the residents of…

05:31.206 --> 05:34.960
and visitors to…
our seaside village is my top priority.

05:35.043 --> 05:38.380
So if a woman is stranded and
needs my help, yes, I'm going to offer it.

05:38.463 --> 05:39.882
Okay, so what is the age cutoff?

05:39.965 --> 05:42.009
Because you once saw me with a flat tire,

05:42.092 --> 05:44.094
- and you kept on driving.
- No, I didn't see you.

05:44.178 --> 05:45.762
Ruth doesn't even have a car.
She walks to work.

05:45.846 --> 05:47.723
Well, I thought she enjoyed the exercise.

05:49.683 --> 05:50.767
Hey, Ruth,

05:51.602 --> 05:53.353
may I offer you a ride tonight?

05:53.979 --> 05:55.522
- Oh, no. Thank you.
- Yeah.

05:56.190 --> 05:57.900
It's the mornings that are hard.

06:10.871 --> 06:13.165
Bases loaded for Detroit. Nobody out.

06:13.665 --> 06:16.126
While Boston's just trying
to minimize the damage.

06:17.503 --> 06:22.341
Detroit scored two in the first,
and now Boston's in another jam here.

06:22.424 --> 06:24.843
Top of the Detroit order
coming up in the fourth.

06:27.930 --> 06:29.806
They needed at least six innings…

06:34.645 --> 06:35.646
Hello.

06:37.439 --> 06:38.440
Hey.

06:40.984 --> 06:42.986
- Am I catching you at a bad time?
- No.

06:44.613 --> 06:45.781
Where you going?

06:47.074 --> 06:49.576
Meeting colleagues. At the Barnabus.

06:50.869 --> 06:52.246
- Colleagues? Colleagues?
- Yeah.

06:53.705 --> 06:57.084
Okay. Well, I'll… I'm going to be home.

06:57.167 --> 06:59.378
- Right, 'cause you're grounded.
- Yeah, of course.

07:07.344 --> 07:09.930
Did you change Dickens Street
to Dickhole Street?

07:11.515 --> 07:12.516
Somebody did that?

07:13.517 --> 07:14.518
That's horrible.

07:18.105 --> 07:19.773
Have a good time with your colleagues.

08:10.824 --> 08:13.744
Somehow it seems

08:13.827 --> 08:18.624
It was all another dream

08:20.042 --> 08:22.461
Soon…

08:30.802 --> 08:32.429
Excuse me, ma'am?

08:36.350 --> 08:37.351
Miss?

08:38.393 --> 08:39.770
Do you need a ride?

08:47.903 --> 08:48.904
Miss?

09:00.707 --> 09:01.708
Hello?

09:09.550 --> 09:10.551
Fuck, fuck.

09:23.105 --> 09:24.398
Fuck.

09:52.634 --> 09:53.844
Did you write that down?

09:54.803 --> 09:57.598
Look, she's probably a homeless woman
who got a free ride on the ferry,

09:57.681 --> 10:01.476
but you should call the mental hospitals
on the mainland, you know, just in case.

10:01.560 --> 10:03.478
And set up a perimeter around the island.

10:04.188 --> 10:05.355
Island has a perimeter.

10:05.439 --> 10:06.648
It's called the ocean.

10:07.816 --> 10:09.985
Okay. I don't know
where your patience is this morning,

10:10.068 --> 10:11.945
but did you write down she was fast?

10:12.654 --> 10:13.655
Yes.

10:15.616 --> 10:16.742
I… Listen, I have…

10:23.207 --> 10:25.792
You sure this wasn't
an animal that did this to you?

10:26.293 --> 10:29.171
No. Why?
Does it look like an animal wound?

10:29.254 --> 10:30.881
Not to me.

10:30.964 --> 10:34.551
Then why would you… Oh, my… I can
still swim in the ocean with this, right?

10:34.635 --> 10:35.844
Of course you can't.

10:36.803 --> 10:38.847
Isn't salt water good for wounds?

10:38.931 --> 10:41.183
Remind me, where did you get your MD?

10:41.266 --> 10:42.518
I'm not doing this with you again.

10:42.601 --> 10:44.269
I have the swim today.
I have to go in the ocean.

10:44.353 --> 10:47.147
You did your residency with Dr. MacArthur,

10:47.231 --> 10:48.941
- right?
- Stop! Stop it! Stop it.

10:49.024 --> 10:51.985
I'm sorry. It's just everything's planned,
people will be waiting.

10:54.655 --> 10:57.449
I mean, who wouldn't show up
for Sunset Cocktails?

10:57.533 --> 11:00.202
It's free drinks and a sunset.

11:00.285 --> 11:01.495
- Tom.
- What?

11:02.204 --> 11:03.455
What happened to your arm?

11:04.331 --> 11:08.460
I got scratched by an elderly woman.

11:09.044 --> 11:10.212
Was she in her 40s?

11:12.339 --> 11:14.258
You know what?
I was trying to do something nice. I…

11:14.341 --> 11:16.844
I saw a woman walking alone late at night…

11:16.927 --> 11:18.095
And I offered her a ride,

11:18.178 --> 11:19.596
she scratched me,
now it won't stop bleeding.

11:19.680 --> 11:21.932
Tom, you just missed a visitor. Mersa.

11:24.226 --> 11:26.895
Marissa? She was here? What did she say?

11:27.646 --> 11:30.357
She asked if you were here. I said no.

11:30.983 --> 11:32.484
Did she leave a number?

11:32.568 --> 11:35.362
No. But… But she said…

11:42.911 --> 11:43.996
- Ruth.
- She said…

11:44.955 --> 11:46.081
- She said…
- Yeah.

11:46.164 --> 11:48.292
"Maybe she'd see you at…

11:49.835 --> 11:52.087
swim…"
There's one more word, just a minute.

11:54.756 --> 11:55.757
Today.

11:56.967 --> 11:57.968
Thanks.

11:59.469 --> 12:02.472
"I officially open the ocean."
"I officially open the ocean."

12:05.601 --> 12:07.561
Sounds like the Sea Hag.

12:08.937 --> 12:10.314
The what?

12:10.397 --> 12:11.607
Your scratch.

12:12.191 --> 12:13.942
Old fishermen's lore, you heard of it?

12:14.902 --> 12:18.238
No, because I can't keep track of
the amount of bullshit this island spews.

12:18.322 --> 12:19.740
No, please don't settle in.

12:19.823 --> 12:22.993
Rosemary, whatever weird tale you're about
to tell me, I don't wanna know.

12:23.076 --> 12:24.453
Story goes,

12:25.037 --> 12:28.624
the Hag targets lonely sailors
and follows them home at night.

12:29.249 --> 12:34.338
She scratches you and she gets some
of your skin under her fingernails

12:34.421 --> 12:37.174
so she can track you down
like a bloodhound.

12:37.841 --> 12:39.218
She's a trickster.

12:39.968 --> 12:43.388
Waits until she's got you alone,
got you weak.

12:56.610 --> 12:58.320
No, you can't have my water.

12:58.403 --> 13:01.907
I don't need to hear the rest of this.
I don't have the time.

13:05.702 --> 13:07.412
Can't do anything right today.

13:27.724 --> 13:28.725
What's wrong?

13:29.268 --> 13:32.437
Apparently, there's no way
to get electricity to the beach.

13:33.897 --> 13:36.024
Why am I just hearing about this now?

13:36.859 --> 13:40.404
Wha… You know, this was Patrici…
Where is she?

13:41.154 --> 13:43.448
Well, I think she's pretty caught up
in her cocktail hour,

13:43.532 --> 13:45.325
but I radioed Garrett
to have him hook us up

13:45.409 --> 13:48.078
to the marina electrical via converter,
and he's on the way.

13:49.413 --> 13:51.456
How fucking long is that gonna take?

13:58.463 --> 14:00.299
No rush, Garrett. Take your time.

14:06.221 --> 14:08.015
He's riding a bicycle?

14:08.974 --> 14:10.601
Jesus Christ.

14:10.684 --> 14:11.685
He stopped.

14:14.563 --> 14:17.191
Oh, no, no, no. Don't…

14:18.567 --> 14:20.194
Oh… Oh, no.

14:22.446 --> 14:23.697
Oh, for fuck's sake.

14:26.617 --> 14:28.493
Don't bring the bike back!

14:38.295 --> 14:39.546
Okay.

14:39.630 --> 14:41.131
- It's working?
- Yeah.

14:41.215 --> 14:43.383
Thank you. Thank you. Thanks…

14:45.886 --> 14:46.970
Hello, everyone.

14:50.432 --> 14:51.517
Hello.

14:51.600 --> 14:52.601
It's not working.

14:57.272 --> 14:59.233
It is my… It is my honor…
It's not working.

14:59.316 --> 15:00.317
I can hear it.

15:01.985 --> 15:03.403
Hello, everyone!

15:05.614 --> 15:10.494
As mayor, it is my honor
to keep this tradition alive.

15:11.036 --> 15:15.290
I would like to welcome
all our new friends joining us this year.

15:16.834 --> 15:19.962
So here's to a safe
and spectacular summer.

15:20.045 --> 15:23.549
I officially open the ocean!

15:31.849 --> 15:35.686
Tonight's the night
We're gonna make it happen

15:36.436 --> 15:37.437
Here we go.

15:37.521 --> 15:41.400
Tonight we'll put
All other things aside

15:42.359 --> 15:43.986
Give in this time and show me…

15:47.698 --> 15:50.742
We're goin' for those pleasures
In the night

17:10.531 --> 17:11.781
Oh, God!

17:13.282 --> 17:15.493
Hey. Come on.

17:15.993 --> 17:17.996
Hey. It's all right, buddy.

18:08.297 --> 18:09.298
Zenith. Cool.

18:10.132 --> 18:12.759
Are you gonna tell me
what the fuck you're doing in my house?

18:13.927 --> 18:16.847
I just thought I'd check in.

18:16.930 --> 18:18.849
Check in. Wellness check?

18:18.932 --> 18:19.933
Okay.

18:21.268 --> 18:26.857
Why don't you just tell me what finally
made you able to ring my doorbell?

18:44.541 --> 18:47.085
Have you ever heard of a hag?

18:47.836 --> 18:52.633
Specifically one that scratches you
and then tracks you down?

18:55.552 --> 18:59.223
Every sailor knows the story of the hag.

19:11.151 --> 19:15.113
Lads say farewell to Ensign Trag

19:16.657 --> 19:21.828
He went to shore and met the Hag

19:22.538 --> 19:27.793
With just one gash betrothed they be

19:28.710 --> 19:34.174
She followed him on land and sea

19:35.425 --> 19:40.097
For if you let her pierce your skin

19:41.723 --> 19:47.396
Betwixt her thighs, your final sin

19:53.735 --> 19:55.988
I don't understand. How do you die?

19:56.822 --> 19:59.157
She crawls into your bed
and sits on your face.

20:03.370 --> 20:05.539
I can't believe I let you
into my head again.

20:06.540 --> 20:08.625
- Goddamn it.
- Wait, Tom. Tom!

20:09.793 --> 20:12.045
When did she get you?

20:13.797 --> 20:14.798
Doesn't matter.

20:15.674 --> 20:18.927
Find a chest,
lock yourself in it from the inside.

20:19.428 --> 20:22.681
- A chest?
- Yeah. Her scratch paralyzes you.

20:22.764 --> 20:24.308
You'll get tired.

20:24.391 --> 20:26.935
By tonight,
you won't be able to lift a finger.

20:27.019 --> 20:30.063
Now, you stay in there for 72 hours.

20:31.190 --> 20:35.068
Till the wound heals,
then she can't track you no more.

20:35.152 --> 20:38.113
Otherwise, she'll hunt you down.

21:08.727 --> 21:10.604
Hello, Gil. PJ.

21:10.687 --> 21:11.688
- What's up.
- Hey.

21:12.189 --> 21:14.566
Hey, they're going to Shawn's house
to stay over.

21:15.359 --> 21:17.653
You're grounded. You're not
even supposed to have friends here.

21:18.153 --> 21:19.154
Oh, yeah.

21:19.738 --> 21:20.948
Yeah.

21:21.031 --> 21:24.034
By the way, some lady named Marissa called

21:24.117 --> 21:27.412
and said that she's going
to the Driftwood now if you're free.

21:29.748 --> 21:31.291
Who's the lucky lady, Mr. Loftis?

21:32.251 --> 21:33.377
She's a friend, PJ.

21:33.460 --> 21:35.587
Hey. I could…

21:36.463 --> 21:39.967
I could go to Shawn's house
to just play a game

21:40.050 --> 21:42.427
with some friends or something,
if you're out of the house.

21:43.971 --> 21:46.265
And you won't be going out
until all hours?

21:46.348 --> 21:49.977
This is a sleepover party?

21:50.060 --> 21:53.272
Yes, it's a sleepover party. Yes.

21:55.023 --> 21:56.024
Okay.

21:57.276 --> 21:58.986
Okay, but please don't do that thing

21:59.069 --> 22:00.696
where you tell me
you're staying at Shawn's

22:00.779 --> 22:03.198
and then tell Shawn's parents you're
staying here. Just stay at Shawn's,

22:03.282 --> 22:04.575
all right? I'm trusting you.

22:05.075 --> 22:06.159
Yes, of course.

22:06.243 --> 22:07.703
We're honest with each other.

22:08.704 --> 22:09.705
Right?

22:15.544 --> 22:17.504
Dude, your dad's gonna get his dick wet.

22:17.588 --> 22:18.589
What?

23:06.637 --> 23:09.264
I'm so sorry
that our food is taking so long.

23:09.765 --> 23:11.642
Oh, my God. You hate this woman.

23:11.725 --> 23:13.977
No, no, I don't. I swear, I don't.

23:15.145 --> 23:17.272
But if I'd known Kathy
was working the Driftwood tonight,

23:17.356 --> 23:18.982
I would have just canceled.

23:19.608 --> 23:20.609
Really?

23:21.193 --> 23:23.695
- Not even a relocation.
- No, call it right off.

23:24.780 --> 23:26.281
I'm not a monster.

23:26.365 --> 23:27.616
No, I'm not,

23:27.699 --> 23:29.826
but I've been watching her
read her paperback all night.

23:30.577 --> 23:31.703
Well, she deserves it.

23:34.665 --> 23:36.166
Thank you, Kathy.

23:39.586 --> 23:40.754
She's my best friend.

23:45.342 --> 23:47.970
You absolutely did not order that.

23:49.304 --> 23:50.889
Yeah, I ordered a sundae.

23:50.973 --> 23:52.224
I know you did.

23:53.016 --> 23:54.476
Wow.

25:07.049 --> 25:08.967
So, do you go out on a lot of dates?

25:09.051 --> 25:10.427
As, you know,

25:11.261 --> 25:12.679
the mayor.

25:13.472 --> 25:15.933
Well, not since Kathy and I split.

25:16.016 --> 25:17.809
It's not a large dating pool.

25:19.061 --> 25:20.687
But you were married, right?

25:23.440 --> 25:24.441
Yes.

25:25.901 --> 25:27.611
How long ago did you separate?

25:29.488 --> 25:32.366
We didn't separate.

25:32.449 --> 25:33.742
She passed away.

25:35.577 --> 25:36.787
I'm so sorry.

25:37.371 --> 25:38.372
Long time ago.

25:42.000 --> 25:43.627
Complications from childbirth.

25:45.379 --> 25:46.797
Hey, squad.

25:46.880 --> 25:49.383
- How do you feel about dessert?
- Could you just give us a minute?

25:49.466 --> 25:50.551
Sure.

25:51.552 --> 25:53.762
- I'm sorry.
- Oh, no, it's fine. It's fine.

25:54.638 --> 25:56.640
I mean, it's just been the two
of us for the most part,

25:56.723 --> 25:59.268
and we've gotten by fine.

26:00.644 --> 26:03.772
I can't imagine what that must have
been like, all on your own.

26:04.731 --> 26:07.025
To just lose someone like that.

26:08.527 --> 26:09.528
That's awful.

26:15.951 --> 26:17.619
Oh, my God.

26:18.120 --> 26:20.038
- What?
- I have sunset cocktails.

26:21.248 --> 26:22.332
Do you have to go?

26:23.125 --> 26:26.295
Well, I think my colleague, Patricia,
would bring a gun to work if I didn't.

26:27.588 --> 26:28.589
I'm sorry.

26:30.174 --> 26:31.175
It's okay.

26:32.509 --> 26:33.719
Did you wanna come?

26:37.639 --> 26:39.433
Is there somewhere else we could go?

26:41.435 --> 26:43.979
It's just this is nice.
I'd love to keep talking.

26:47.024 --> 26:49.109
Maybe we could go to your house?

26:58.368 --> 27:01.079
I'm sorry, is that weird? I'm sorry.

27:02.247 --> 27:03.248
I'm sorry.

27:03.332 --> 27:06.210
I swear, I don't usually invite myself
over to a man's house.

27:06.710 --> 27:08.420
No, no, of course. It's just…

27:10.756 --> 27:11.965
Tonight's not the best.

27:12.466 --> 27:14.218
Yeah. No, I get it.

27:27.022 --> 27:28.357
Wait a second.

27:28.440 --> 27:30.150
You've never been to Boston?

27:30.234 --> 27:31.235
- That's insane.
- No, no, no.

27:31.318 --> 27:34.279
I mean, I have, but yeah,
these guys have never left the island.

27:34.363 --> 27:37.991
What? You've never even left the island?

27:38.075 --> 27:39.535
No way.

27:41.203 --> 27:42.829
You guys do this shit in Boston?

27:55.926 --> 27:58.136
Yes, we do that in Boston.

28:04.101 --> 28:05.269
Reverend Bryce?

28:12.067 --> 28:13.652
There is evil here.

28:50.898 --> 28:52.191
Well, Tom.

28:52.274 --> 28:55.194
I don't know where you are,
but I am at the event…

28:57.029 --> 28:58.488
that you said you would be at!

29:03.202 --> 29:04.828
Loftis, pick up.

29:06.038 --> 29:09.041
If she's not inside yet,
she's gonna find a way.

29:10.834 --> 29:12.628
You won't be able to fight her off…

29:57.256 --> 29:58.340
Hello?

29:59.216 --> 30:00.467
Hi, it's me.

30:02.177 --> 30:04.304
We took a shot and they dropped me off.

30:05.597 --> 30:07.224
How did you know where I live?

30:09.268 --> 30:11.395
Someone from your office told me.

30:13.772 --> 30:16.900
I haven't seen any of your friends and…

30:17.943 --> 30:22.698
and no one in town has mentioned
anything about a bachelorette party.

30:25.617 --> 30:29.288
I mean, you can meet them tomorrow
if you want.

30:32.332 --> 30:33.834
Aren't you going to let me in?

30:34.626 --> 30:36.128
Why are you asking like that?

30:39.089 --> 30:40.174
Like what?

30:41.091 --> 30:43.510
Okay, I think I am getting
mixed signals here.

30:44.178 --> 30:45.345
Can we just talk?

30:45.929 --> 30:47.055
No.

30:48.390 --> 30:50.893
No, I know what you are.

31:17.628 --> 31:20.881
- Well, that was humiliating.
- Why? What happened?

31:42.528 --> 31:43.529
Shit.

32:18.939 --> 32:20.190
Why are you so groggy?

32:23.235 --> 32:24.236
I don't know.

32:32.119 --> 32:33.787
I thought you went to work.

32:36.999 --> 32:38.000
Not yet.

32:43.839 --> 32:44.923
Thank you.

32:45.007 --> 32:46.008
You're welcome.

33:39.937 --> 33:41.522
Come on. Come on. Come on.

34:49.047 --> 34:50.465
Hey.

35:19.494 --> 35:21.079
Why is this happening?

35:24.124 --> 35:25.209
I don't know.

35:25.792 --> 35:27.878
You just survive.

35:36.094 --> 35:37.304
Come on.

35:39.640 --> 35:42.017
Tom. It's Bryce.

35:43.727 --> 35:44.728
I heard it.

35:45.604 --> 35:48.524
I'm so sorry. God forgive me.

35:57.407 --> 36:00.410
Rescue station one.
This is Sheriff Clemmons.

36:00.494 --> 36:02.037
All available fire and rescue.

36:02.955 --> 36:04.331
Patricia's cocktails.

36:04.414 --> 36:06.250
I don't know what the fuck is going on!
